From: lighter <build@invalid>
Subject: virtio_balloon: compound units from the largest aligned order down to a host page, movable and migratable

The balloon inflates in compound units, never in single pages. On Apple
silicon the host page is 16 KiB and the guest's is 4 KiB, and a balloon that
hands back single guest pages hands back almost nothing the host can
release: only an aligned run of four is a host page, and a fragmented guest
yields few. Measured: three quarters of a gigabyte inflated, the host's
footprint unmoved, the guest's cache gone. So the smallest unit is an
order-2 compound page, sixteen aligned kilobytes, always releasable.

Since 0.7.2 the largest unit is tried first: a whole pageblock (order 9,
2 MiB), the order halving until the allocator gives one, down to 2. A
balloon of four gigabytes is then a couple of thousand whole pageblocks
rather than a quarter million 16 KiB islands, so what the guest keeps
stays compactable and reportable, and the host releases long aligned runs.

And the units are movable pages (CONFIG_BALLOON_COMPACTION): allocated
from ZONE_MOVABLE, so the balloon never takes the kernel's own zones, and
migrated by compaction as compound folios. Until 0.7.1 the units were
unmovable and came from the kernel-usable zones; with a 4 GiB balloon in
them a 16 GiB guest had four gigabytes for its kernel, its vsock buffers
and its slab, and stalled (the M5, 2026-09-20: 478k allocation stalls,
the docker socket's stream lost, a build's session with it). Linux 6.18's
migration already isolates a compound movable_ops page by its head,
allocates the destination at the source's order and hands both heads to
the driver; the driver's part is to tell the host in units, which the
pfn array is sized for (1024, a 2 MiB unit twice), and to keep its
accounting in units of whatever order each page is.

---
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
@@ -25,7 +25,36 @@
  * page units.
  */
 #define VIRTIO_BALLOON_PAGES_PER_PAGE (unsigned int)(PAGE_SIZE >> VIRTIO_BALLOON_PFN_SHIFT)
-#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_ARRAY_PFNS_MAX 256
+/*
+ * lighter: the balloon inflates in compound units, never in single pages.
+ * On Apple silicon the host page is 16 KiB and the guest's is 4 KiB, and a
+ * balloon that hands back single guest pages hands back almost nothing the
+ * host can release: only an aligned run of four is a host page, and a
+ * fragmented guest yields few (measured: three quarters of a gigabyte
+ * inflated, the host's footprint unmoved, the guest's cache gone). So the
+ * smallest unit is an order-2 compound page, sixteen aligned kilobytes,
+ * always releasable.
+ *
+ * And the largest unit is tried first: a whole pageblock (order 9, 2 MiB),
+ * the order halving until the allocator gives one, down to 2. A balloon of
+ * four gigabytes is then a couple of thousand whole pageblocks rather than
+ * a quarter million 16 KiB islands, so what the guest keeps stays
+ * compactable and reportable, and the host releases long aligned runs.
+ *
+ * Units are movable pages (CONFIG_BALLOON_COMPACTION): allocated from
+ * ZONE_MOVABLE, so the balloon never takes the kernel's own zones — with a
+ * 4 GiB balloon in them a 16 GiB guest stalled on the M5 (2026-09-20) —
+ * and migrated by compaction as compound folios. The kernel's migration
+ * allocates the destination at the source's order and hands both heads to
+ * migratepage below, which tells the host in units; a unit at the
+ * pageblock order is never a compaction candidate, since it already is
+ * what compaction makes. The balloon's accounting stays in 4 KiB pfns as
+ * the device expects, and a unit's pfns are told to the host together.
+ */
+#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_UNIT_MIN_ORDER 2
+#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_UNIT_MAX_ORDER 9
+#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_PFNS_PER_MIN_UNIT (VIRTIO_BALLOON_PAGES_PER_PAGE << VIRTIO_BALLOON_UNIT_MIN_ORDER)
+#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_ARRAY_PFNS_MAX 1024
 /* Maximum number of (4k) pages to deflate on OOM notifications. */
 #define VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NR_PAGES 256
 #define VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NOTIFY_PRIORITY 80
@@ -143,6 +172,12 @@
 	return pfn * VIRTIO_BALLOON_PAGES_PER_PAGE;
 }
 
+/* lighter: the balloon pfns one compound unit spans. */
+static unsigned int unit_pfns(struct page *page)
+{
+	return VIRTIO_BALLOON_PAGES_PER_PAGE << compound_order(page);
+}
